===Etymology===
From {{etyl|VL.|it}} {{term|ceresia|lang=la}}, from the neuter plural of {{etyl|LL.|it}} {{term|ceresium|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|la|it}} {{term|cerasium|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|it}} {{term|κεράσιον||cherry|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}, from {{etyl|grc|it}} {{term|κερασός||[[bird cherry]]|lang=el}}, ultimately possibly of {{etyl|ine-ana|it}} origin. Alternatively from ''[[ciliegio]]'', ''[[ciriegio]]'' (Tuscan), from {{etyl|LL.|it}} ''ceresus'', from {{etyl|la|it}} {{term|cerasus|lang=la}}. See also {{term|cerasa|lang=it}}.

